Use this checklist to protect your academic work and personal finances:
​Secure UPI Transactions: Never enter your UPI PIN to receive money; it is only required for sending. Always verify the recipient's name before confirming.
​Enable Biometrics: Use fingerprint or Face ID for all banking and payment apps to prevent unauthorized access if your phone is misplaced.
​Avoid Public Wi-Fi for Sensitive Tasks: Use your mobile data for banking or accessing university portals; public networks are hotspots for data interception.
​Use Unique Passwords: Use a password manager to ensure your university ID and personal emails have strong, different credentials.
​Verify Recruitment Links: Be skeptical of "internship" offers via WhatsApp or Telegram that ask for registration fees or personal documents.
​Enable MFA: Activate Multi-Factor Authentication on your Google and social media accounts to block 99% of automated hacks.
​Audit App Permissions: Regularly check which apps have access to your camera, contacts, and location.
​Watch for Deepfakes: Be cautious of urgent "emergency" calls from friends asking for money; verify their identity through a separate channel.
​Report Cybercrime: If you face fraud, immediately call the national helpline at 1930 or visit www.cybercrime.gov.in.
